      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "Glimepiride, the closest structural analogue sharing the sulfonylurea, phenethyl linker, cyclohexyl urea, and heteroaromatic amide features, has an absolute oral bioavailability of 97% in healthy volunteers, strongly supporting high F for the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C16"],
      "claim": "Tolbutamide, a simpler sulfonylurea with the same central sulfonylurea pharmacophore, has an absolute oral bioavailability of 0.85 in humans, supporting high F.",
